    merge DF-SPECLANG-016: load the shipped cascades migration (v3) so MCP cascade tools stop 500ing
    
    003_cascades.sql shipped in two places but no migration runner read it: migrations.ts
    only declared versions 1 (initial_schema) and 2, so the cascades table was never
    created and cascade_status / dashboard / status / SSE tools died on
    "no such table: cascades".
    
    The worker added an idempotent version-3 cascades migration whose column set is the
    union of what the consumers actually touch (cascade_id/depth/status, root_trigger,
    created_at, started_at, converged_at, root_trigger_file) with indexes on
    status/started_at/converged_at/root_trigger_file, synced the spec DDL and
    migrations.spec.md to the same column set, and re-emitted migrations.js because
    index.ts resolves "./migrations.js" rather than the .ts (without it the version is
    inert at runtime).
    
    Regression coverage: tests/db/cascades-migration.test.ts (194 lines) boots
    SpecLangDB on a fresh temp DB file, asserts the table and every consumer column
    exists after initialize(), and pins the .sql file to the same column set;
    tests/db.test.ts pins the migration count/version.
    
    Gates: npm run build rc=0; full vitest suite green in the merged tree (1865 passed
    | 58 skipped, 21.69s baseline re-measured after the merge). The worktree run showed
    one environmental failure in tests/ci/ci005-precommit-hook.test.ts because a linked
    worktree's .git is a file, so the hook lookup misses; it passes in a normal checkout.
    npm run lint stays red repo-wide (ESLint vs TypeScript 7 = QA-SPECLANG-006), unrelated.
    
    Worker: openai/gpt-6.1-terra @ xkiro, worktree /home/kara/worktrees/speclang-DF-SPECLANG-016, commit 1424d92d.
    
